wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc = An Arbites department scene source. Put seated actors on their chair tile and the sleeper on a bunk; marker rotation sets the resting facing.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-snore = ZZZ...
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cuffs-name = detainee's handcuffs
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cuffs-desc = Handcuffs worn by a detainee in the Arbites department.
ent-HandcuffsWH40KFootfallScene = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cuffs-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cuffs-desc }
wh40k-footfall-arbites-chief-laws-choice = What laws and rules apply here?
wh40k-footfall-arbites-chief-laws = The Lex Imperialis is not a price list, and an impressive name earns no discount. A visitor's reminder: do not threaten people, take others' property, obstruct detentions or enter restricted rooms without clearance. A reminder, not the full code. Disputes need circumstances and evidence; the colour of someone's armour does not deliver a verdict.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-chief-report-choice = How do I report an offence?
wh40k-footfall-arbites-chief-report = Start with reception: your name, the place, the time and everyone involved. Recordings, witnesses, manifests; anything that lets us check your words rather than merely believe them. For an immediate threat, call the patrol. To help on an assignment, ask for work here; its terms and target are recorded separately. An improvised execution does not qualify as unusually swift investigation.

wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-name = Arbites detective
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-desc = An Arbites uniform under a grey coat. Cross-checks testimony against a manifest.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-marker = Arbites detective spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-line-1 = So the crate walked out by itself. Your fingerprints on its handles must be from trying to bring it back?
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-line-2 = The recording shows you waving a pass at the porter. The pass is forged; your enthusiasm is authentic.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-line-3 = The report already contains 'accidentally', 'cannot recall' and 'it just happened'. For variety, try a time and a place.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-line-4 = You can give a statement outside. Someone is giving one here already. Please do not coach our expert on self-propelled crates.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesDetective = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesDetective = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-detective-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-name = Detained porter
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-desc = Sits handcuffed, carefully avoiding the manifest.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-marker = Detained porter spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-line-1 = I did not steal the crate. I escorted it. It seemed very determined to reach the exit.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-line-2 = The job came with a pass. Turns out the work was real and the pass was an artistic interpretation.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-line-3 = I explained the fingerprints: the crate was slippery. If I had not held on, it might have escaped as well.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-line-4 = Here as a witness? Confirm I have been sitting here the entire time. Admittedly, not the time he is asking about.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesDetainee = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesDetainee = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-detainee-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-name = Arbites recruit
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-desc = Light Arbites armour, helmet off. Takes excessively diligent briefing notes.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-marker = Arbites recruit spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-line-1 = Noted: introduce yourself, then request documents. Got that backwards last shift. They asked for mine first.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-line-2 = The sergeant said not to lose my head. I left the helmet in my locker, so at least I know where that is.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-line-3 = The textbook says the detainee cooperates. Ours seems to have a newer edition.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-line-4 = Still taking notes. If righteous indignation could fill forms, the queue would be shorter.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesRookieOne = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesRookieOne = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookieone-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-name = Helmeted recruit
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-desc = Sits in full Minoris gear, trying to look experienced.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-marker = Helmeted recruit spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-line-1 = Kept my helmet on for briefing. If asked, it is readiness. If not, it hides a yawn nicely.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-line-2 = Remembered the key point: check the fuse with your eyes, not your finger. Wish someone had stressed just how key that was.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-line-3 = No questions. One clarification: why is 'quiet patrol' pencilled into the roster?
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-line-4 = The instructor says armour cannot replace a brain. Looking at repair costs, the department needs both.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesRookieTwo = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesRookieTwo = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookietwo-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-name = Recruit with a notebook
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-desc = Light armour and a black cap. Underlines the awkward questions.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-marker = Recruit with a notebook spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-line-1 = Lost your papers? Go to reception. Reception lost your statement? That is called archiving.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-line-2 = Asked whether snoring counts as disorder. The sergeant looked at the cell cameras and told me not to invent work.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-line-3 = Third run through the search rules. Think they are searching what remains inside our heads now.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-line-4 = Everything on duty must be orderly. Before my first patrol I already have three lists of what might not be.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesRookieThree = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesRookieThree = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-rookiethree-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-name = Arbites briefing officer
wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-desc = Medius armour, an officer's cap and the shift briefing clipboard.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-marker = Arbites briefing officer spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-line-1 = Recruits: lower weapons, keep the passage clear, write names legibly. The last one currently costs us more time than the first two.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-line-2 = Shouting is not evidence. Even when you do it and know the regulations extremely well.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-line-3 = If someone vanishes from a camera, check the next screen first. Rule out a door before declaring a warp breach.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-line-4 = A detention needs grounds and a report. 'I did not like him' is grounds to reconsider your report.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesInstructor = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesInstructor = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-instructor-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-name = Arbites reception clerk
wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-desc = Light armour and a black cap. Receives visitors and statements.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-marker = Arbites reception clerk spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-line-1 = Complaints here, testimony to the detective, assignments to Hawkins. If it is all three, start with your name.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-line-2 = Describe what happened, where and when. I can write down 'everyone saw it', but cannot interview everyone at once.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-line-3 = List missing items one at a time. Faith in humanity does not go on the inventory; stores will not accept it.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-line-4 = Queue here. Cutting through the armoury will not help; they issue something rather different.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesReceptionist = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesReceptionist = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-receptionist-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-name = Entrance camera operator
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-desc = Helmet off. Checks entrance cameras against the duty log.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-marker = Entrance camera operator spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-line-1 = Entrance is quiet. The fellow reading the sign a third time is either very law-abiding or hunting for small print.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-line-2 = The camera shows the passage, not intentions. For intentions we have a detective and an uncomfortable chair.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-line-3 = Please stop waving at the lens. I see you. The recording now shows you obstructing the view very amicably.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-line-4 = Reception takes statements. I only receive pictures, and even those sometimes freeze.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesCameraEntrance = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesCameraEntrance = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraentrance-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-name = Department camera operator
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-desc = An Arbites in a beret watching the inner passages and armoury entrance.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-marker = Department camera operator spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-line-1 = Order inside: recruits sitting, armourer counting, prisoners pretending to have no plans.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-line-2 = Same prisoner studying the door on the next screen again. Admirable persistence, questionable career direction.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-line-3 = I log who enters the armoury. Anyone leaving with extras gets something more personal than camera attention.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-line-4 = Everything looks quieter on a recording. It is the only pleasant way to watch our briefings.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesCameraOffice = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesCameraOffice = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-cameraoffice-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-name = Arbites armourer
wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-desc = Sorts flashbangs while standing. An orderly workbench and a thoroughly suspicious expression.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-marker = Arbites armourer spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-line-1 = Pin present, casing intact, number recorded. A rattling grenade is not an invitation to shake harder.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-line-2 = Flashbangs are signed out. Someone tried 'for a celebration' under intended use. I declined.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-line-3 = Do not touch that row. I have counted it; recruits use the 'seemed enough earlier' system.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-line-4 = Return grenades with their pins. An account of where the pin went does not make the inventory complete.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesArmourer = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesArmourer = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-armourer-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-name = Arbites warden
wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-desc = Reinforced Arbites armour and a warden's cap. Watches cells and the custody register.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-marker = Arbites warden spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-line-1 = One sleeps, two make plans. The sleeper is the only one keeping to his schedule.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-line-2 = Your sentence does not change with how meaningfully you stare at the door. I checked the register.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-line-3 = Parcels go through reception. We will notice a file in a loaf; our bread is softer than inventors expect.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-line-4 = I open on orders and check the register. If the entry is not yours, neither is the release.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesWarden = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesWarden = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-warden-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-name = Sleeping prisoner
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-desc = Asleep on a bunk in prison clothes. Snoring stands in for all objections.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-marker = Sleeping prisoner spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-line-1 = Mmm... Roll call after breakfast... Hrrr...
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-line-2 = Good plan... Wake me when we are outside... Hrr...
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-line-3 = Five more minutes... Tell the court too...
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-line-4 = Hrrr... I did not take the door...

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesPrisonerSleeper = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesPrisonerSleeper = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonersleeper-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-name = Scheming prisoner
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-desc = Studies wall seams with the air of someone who almost has an exit plan.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-marker = Scheming prisoner spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-line-1 = Simple plan: wait for the warden to get distracted. So far he only gets distracted by our plans.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-line-2 = My neighbour is meant to watch the passage. He watches for lunch instead. The man has unshakeable priorities.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-line-3 = The third promised to help after his nap. Promised yesterday too. Our escape is becoming a long-term project.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-line-4 = No tunnel. I am just checking the wall quality. Free of charge, I might add.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesPrisonerPlanner = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesPrisonerPlanner = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerplanner-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-name = Prisoner lookout
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-desc = Heard the escape plan and now watches meal deliveries particularly closely.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-marker = Prisoner lookout spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-line-1 = He says 'wait for a distraction'. I asked: before lunch or after? Strategy should not interfere with nutrition.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-line-2 = I can see the passage. The warden can see me seeing it. Mutual surveillance instead of escape.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-line-3 = If the sleeper wakes, he will ask about breakfast first. He will only accept freedom with rations.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-line-4 = We discuss architecture. Such as why the door is so discouraging from this side.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesPrisonerLookout = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesPrisonerLookout = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-prisonerlookout-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-name = Shotgun Arbites guard
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-desc = Medius armour and helmet. Guards the passage with a shotgun.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-marker = Shotgun Arbites guard spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-line-1 = Passage clear. Leave it that way behind you.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-line-2 = Keep papers separate from weapons. It makes checks considerably calmer.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-line-3 = The shotgun is not part of the argument. I strongly suggest keeping it that way.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-line-4 = Looking for the chief? His office. Looking for grounds for detention? You are standing rather close.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesGuardOne = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesGuardOne = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardone-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-name = Heavy Arbites guard
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-desc = Full Majoris gear. On guard with a compact stub weapon.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-marker = Heavy Arbites guard spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-line-1 = Yes, the armour is heavy. No, it does not move my post any closer to the exit.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-line-2 = I guard the door, not your secret. Tell the detective the secret if necessary.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-line-3 = Do not test whether your confidence is tougher than my helmet. Confidence usually comes off worse.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-line-4 = A quiet passage makes a good shift. Let us not look for exceptions out of curiosity.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesGuardTwo = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesGuardTwo = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardtwo-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }

wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-name = Veteran Arbites guard
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-desc = Arbites armour and a beret, helmet off. Prefers a good look at someone before writing a report.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-marker = Veteran Arbites guard spawn
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-line-1 = Start with an explanation. It takes less room in the log than the consequences.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-line-2 = My helmet is off, my duty is not. Same reason to lower your voice.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-line-3 = Everyone entering is innocent of things we have not asked about yet. Do not rush to expand the questions.
wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-line-4 = You may argue with the sign. You may not block the passage while doing so.

ent-MobWH40KFootfallArbitesGuardThree = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallArbitesGuardThree = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-guardthree-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-arbites-department-marker-desc }
